# E2a del piano interlocutore-di-frontiera (§9.9-9.10): la sufficienza.
# Banco scritto PRIMA della cura, su KB viva `agi`. Misura tre cose distinte:
# lo STATO di un requisito (confermato / confutato / ancora aperto) deciso da
# un limite quando il valore esatto manca; il RESIDUO tipato che dice quale
# condizione manca; la CONDOTTA (confermare o chiedere) insegnata parlando e
# ritrattabile. Le premesse sono lezioni: non provano conoscenza del mondo.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test un limite conferma: senza preferenza lo stato e' deciso ma la mossa no]
!timeout 6
> calculate ready by adding arrival and transfer
<~ ready
> transfer is never below 0
> the arrival of train is 10
> for train the ready must be at least 9
> can I complete train?
<~ choose
<~ confirming
<~ asking
<! What is

[test la lezione di sufficienza sceglie la conferma, con il sostegno detto]
!timeout 6
> prefer confirming the check to asking questions when a bound settles it
<~ preference
> can I complete train?
<~ satisfied
<~ at least 10
<! What is

[test lo stesso limite confuta un requisito opposto]
!timeout 6
> forget the requirement for train on ready
> for train the ready must be at most 9
> prefer explaining obstacles to asking questions when a requirement fails
> can I complete train?
<~ No: ready is at least 10
<~ at most 9
<! What is

[test ancora indeciso: la domanda porta la soglia, non solo la casella]
!timeout 6
> forget the requirement for train on ready
> for train the ready must be at most 11
> can I complete train?
<~ What is the transfer of train?
<~ transfer must be at most 1
> what remains for train?
<~ transfer must be at most 1

[test la frontiera segue il confronto: non stretto passa a 1, stretto no]
!timeout 6
> it is 1
<~ transfer is 1
<~ satisfied
> forget the requirement for train on ready
> for train the ready must be less than 11
> can I complete train?
<~ No: ready reaches 11
<~ less than 11
> the transfer of train is 0.5
> can I complete train?
<~ satisfied

[test il minimo insegnato e poi ritirato: la conclusione compare e scompare]
!timeout 6
> the arrival of bus is 10
> for bus the ready must be at least 9
> can I complete bus?
<~ satisfied
<~ at least 10
> forget that transfer is never below 0
> can I complete bus?
<~ What is the transfer of bus?
<! satisfied
> transfer is never below 0
> can I complete bus?
<~ satisfied

[test due dati ignoti: residuo congiunto, i limiti dei singoli non certificano la somma]
!timeout 6
> calculate arrival by adding departure and duration
> for boat the arrival must be at most 10
> can I complete boat?
<~ departure and duration
<~ departure plus duration must be at most 10
> departure is never above 6
> duration is never above 6
> can I complete boat?
<! satisfied
<~ ?
> forget that duration is never above 6
> duration is never above 4
> can I complete boat?
<~ satisfied
<~ at most 10

[test un impedimento basta per il no; il residuo resta dovuto a chi chiede tutto]
!timeout 6
> calculate load by adding cargo and packaging
> packaging is never below 0
> the cargo of van is 12
> for van the load must be at most 10
> for van the fuel must be at least 5
> can I complete van?
<~ No: load is at least 12
<! What is
> what remains for van?
<~ load is at least 12
<~ fuel must be at least 5

[test cambiare una premessa dopo la risposta invalida la conclusione]
!timeout 6
> the fuel of van is 6
> the cargo of van is 9
> can I complete van?
<~ What is the packaging of van?
<~ packaging must be at most 1
> it is 1
<~ satisfied
> the cargo of van is 10
> can I complete van?
<~ No: load reaches 11

[test una regola nuova dopo una prova riapre completezza e conflitto]
!timeout 6
> calculate fuel by adding tank and reserve
> the tank of van is 2
> the reserve of van is 2
> prefer explaining obstacles to asking questions when the data disagree
> can I complete van?
<~ fuel comes out as
<~ different rules

[test ablazione parlata della condotta di sufficienza]
!timeout 6
> the arrival of tram is 10
> for tram the ready must be at least 9
> forget that preference for confirming the check over asking questions when a bound settles it
> can I complete tram?
<~ choose
<! satisfied
> prefer confirming the check to asking questions when a bound settles it
> can I complete tram?
<~ satisfied

[test il tetto si insegna anche per parafrasi, e il verso stretto viaggia nel residuo]
# il lettore «x means y» costa 7-8 s da solo (non di questo circuito)
!timeout 10
> x never exceeds y means x is never above y
> the arrival of cab is 10
> for cab the ready must be more than 12
> can I complete cab?
<~ What is the transfer of cab?
<~ transfer must be more than 2
> transfer is never above 1
> can I complete cab?
<~ No: ready is at most 11
<~ more than 12
> forget that transfer is never above 1
> forget that x never exceeds y means x is never above y

[test un ruolo senza requisiti non e' un successo]
!timeout 6
> what remains for holiday?
<! satisfied
